==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒkl̩/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkəl|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
[[File:Coque blanche (Cerastoderma edule).jpg|thumb|Cockles]]
From {{inh|en|enm|cokel}}, {{m|enm|cokkel}}, {{m|enm|kokkel}}, {{m|enm|cocle}}, of uncertain origin. Perhaps a diminutive of {{der|en|enm|cok|t=cockle}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cocc}} (found in {{m|ang|sǣcocc|t=cockle}}) {{suffix|en||le}}; or perhaps from {{der|en|fro|coquille}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{m|la|*cocchilia}}, form of {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|conchylia}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|κογχύλιον}}, diminutive of {{m|grc|κογχύλη||mussel}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*konkho}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various [[edible]] [[European]] [[bivalve]] [[mollusk]]s, of the [[family]] [[Cardiidae]], having [[heart]]-[[shaped]] [[shell]]s.
# The [[shell]] of such a mollusk.
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} One’s [[innermost]] [[feeling]]s (only in the expression “[[warm the cockles of one's heart|the cockles of one’s heart]]”).
# {{lb|en|directly from French coquille}} A [[wrinkle]], [[pucker]]
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A defect in [[sheepskin]]; firm dark [[nodule]]s caused by the bites of [[ked]]s on live sheep
# {{lb|en|mining|UK|Cornwall}} The [[mineral]] black tourmaline or [[schorl]].
#: {{rfquotek|Raymond}}
# {{lb|en|UK}} The fire chamber of a [[furnace]].
#: {{rfquotek|Knight}}
# {{lb|en|UK}} A [[kiln]] for drying [[hops]]; an [[oast]].
#: {{rfquotek|Knight}}
# {{lb|en|UK}} The dome of a heating furnace.
#: {{rfquotek|Knight}}

